 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The imperfetto tense",
     "texto": [
      "It is used to describe continuing situations, physical or emotional states and habits in the past. It corresponds to English «I was», «I was speaking» and «I used to live».",
      "Unlike the passato prossimo, the imperfetto doesn't say when the action ended or present it as a completed event."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Regular formation",
     "texto": [
      "Take the infinitive stem and add the endings: **-avo, -avi, -ava, -avamo, -avate, -avano** for -are (*parlavo*); **-evo, -evi, -eva, -evamo, -evate, -evano** for -ere (*leggevo*); **-ivo, -ivi, -iva, -ivamo, -ivate, -ivano** for -ire (*dormivo*)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Common irregular verbs",
     "texto": [
      "**Essere**: *ero, eri, era, eravamo, eravate, erano*. **Fare**: *facevo, facevi, faceva, facevamo, facevate, facevano*. **Dire**: *dicevo, dicevi, diceva...*. **Bere**: *bevevo, bevevi, beveva...*."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
